From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: send PMF peers to WMI-TLV firmware

ath10k flags a peer as PMF in its peer assoc only when firmware-N.bin
advertises ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT, and the WCN3990 firmware-5.bin
in linux-firmware does not. A WCN3990 associated with a PMF network then
never tells the firmware that the peer uses PMF, although every WCN3990
firmware has PMF offload, and that firmware drops ADDBA requests on the
mismatch ("ADDBA Req dropped WEP:%d MFP_SUPPORT:%d").

The vendor driver, qcacld-3.0, sets WMI_PEER_PMF whenever PMF was
negotiated, and so do ath11k and ath12k. Do the same for WMI-TLV
firmware, and keep the feature check for the other WMI branches.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -2253,9 +2253,11 @@
 		arg->peer_flags |= ar->wmi.peer_flags->need_gtk_2_way;
 	}
 
+	/* WMI-TLV firmware takes PMF peers whatever firmware-N.bin says */
 	if (sta->mfp &&
-	    test_bit(ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT,
-		     ar->running_fw->fw_file.fw_features)) {
+	    (ar->running_fw->fw_file.wmi_op_version == ATH10K_FW_WMI_OP_VERSION_TLV ||
+	     test_bit(ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT,
+		      ar->running_fw->fw_file.fw_features))) {
 		arg->peer_flags |= ar->wmi.peer_flags->pmf;
 	}
 }
